This is a project of AI resume builder Rezynt with a separated frontend and backend architecture.

All the content, comments, docstings, ui elements - in English.

rezynt/
├── backend/         # Backend server directory
├── frontend/        # Frontend application directory
├── nginx/           # Nginx service configuration for deployment
├── .github/         # github action workflows configuration for CI/CD
└── .git/            # Git version control

Each meaningfull folder cintains `spec.xml` file with feature description and technical specifications for this piece of code. Always use this files to understand the code structure in the corresponding folder.

When you change the code, you MUST update the corresponding `spec.xml` so that it reflects the present code state.

When you add some functionality described in `spec.xml` files, use as few changes as possible, just add new functionality and keep the structure as was.

I run all the code on the remote server. NEVER try to find docker containers or other prod-specific services locally, they all are on the remote server. Instead, just analyze docker compose, .github/build.yaml and other deploy files.

<backend>
    Use python classes whereever possible.
    Make as short and simple code as possible for the proposed functionality, do not expand functionality without approve from user. 

    Use uv for packages management.
    `uv add package` for adding new packages

    For alembic commands use a prefix: $env:PYTHONPATH='.';
    For example:
    ```powershell
    $env:PYTHONPATH='.'; alembic upgrade head
    ```

    <tech_stack>
        <framework>FastAPI</framework>
        <orm>SQLAlchemy + Alembic для миграций</orm>
        <validation>Pydantic</validation>
        <api_docs>Swagger UI (встроенный в FastAPI)</api_docs>
        <auth>PyJWT</auth>
        <async_tasks>Celery + Redis</async_tasks>
        <storage>MinIO</storage>
        <database>PostgreSQL</database>
    </tech_stack>
</backend>

<frontend>
All the texts should be stored in the `i18n` folder. 
Always use yarn + vite, not npm.
Never build and start app by yourself: i always do it manually.
All the colors should be stored in theme.ts file
</frontend>
